{"agent":"bg25","data":{"budget":"","claim":"The gate-status why note only surfaces a recorded reason for unavailable/partial outcomes; a FAILED gate reason loses to the queued-elapsed note.","dedupe":{"answer":"new","candidates":[{"id":"B46339c052b","score":0.583019613},{"id":"fix-B46339c052b","score":0.548762107}],"score":0.583019613},"falsifier":"A FAILED gate whose record has both a non-empty reason and waited_s greater than 0 renders its reason in gate status.","item":"fix-B-gate-status-hides-failed-reason","mechanism":"_why_notes merges _queued_notes (queued Xm of Ym elapsed) with _unavailable_reasons, which skips any outcome not in (unavailable, partial); so failed never sets the why note and only the queued text remains.","probe":"test_a_failed_gates_reason_wins_over_the_queued_note: on unfixed code _why_notes returns the queued 48m of 81m elapsed note instead of the reason.","probe_output":"FAILED: assert ci==queued 48m of 81m elapsed != ci==1 test failed: tests/test_x.py","question":"Why does ddflow gate status show a failed ci as queued and drop its failure reason?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"ee08a197a3bb310851812da7d","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":148404,"schema":1,"subject":"R5aa1d3e1aa","ts":"2026-11-07T09:14:51.755509Z"}
