{"agent":"bg25","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The function now unconditionally emits a note for every `failed` row, falling back to `\"no reason was recorded\"` when `rec.reason` is empty. In `_why_notes` this dict is merged after `_queued_notes`, so a failed gate with queue evidence but no recorded reason loses its queued note. For example, `_why_notes(NS(gates={\"ci\": NS(reason=\"\", evidence={\"waited_s\": 2880, \"elapsed_s\": 4860})}), [(\"ci\", \"failed\")])` returns `{\"ci\": \"no reason was recorded\"}` instead of `{\"ci\": \"queued 48m of 81m elapsed\"}`. Unlike `unavailable`/`partial`, `failed` outcomes are not made mandatory-reason outcomes by this change, so the real queue status is hidden whenever a failed gate has no optional recorded reason.","digest":"014c0a4f50b74abf","location":"ddflow/services/gates/reasons.py:_unavailable_reasons","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/gates/reasons.py:_unavailable_reasons"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":4767,"diff_sha":"a88a71a533b2e9812b9de393e9b9d3bab2d3bb5442fc0a3b401ceba29eae9a37","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.8,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"aaf165b9d61e4d60","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-gate-status-hides-failed-reason.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261107T092304Z-5fd1d0c8.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"b37a5ef11f7747018bc4fe5e0193dd3ff2a11c24","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/gates/reasons.py":"100644 6e17b46be83c7daa66e60f82bd4a130f386c5d59","ddflow/services/gates/status_notes.py":"100644 e612d2bbb062944915a81a42fdee9d67480ad48f","tests/test_gate_status_failed_reason.py":"100644 66232270ce4514